                                                           'binding to the same extent as original '
                                                           'signatures, and the Parties consent to '
                                                           'the use of electronic records and '
                                                           'signatures under the New Jersey '
                                                           'Uniform Electronic Transactions Act, '
                                                           'N.J.S.A. 12A:12-1 et seq., and the '
                                                           'federal Electronic Signatures in '
                                                           'Global and National Commerce Act, 15 '
                                                           'U.S.C. § 7001 et seq. Neither Party '
                                                           'shall contest the validity or '
                                                           'admissibility of this Agreement on the '
                                                           'basis of electronic execution.',
                                                           '23.7\u2003Further Assurances.\u2003'
                                                           'Each Party shall execute and deliver '
                                                           'such further documents and take such '
                                                           'further actions as the other Party '
                                                           'reasonably requests to carry out this '
                                                           'Agreement, including documents '
                                                           'reasonably required by a Capital '
                                                           'Source to evidence Qualified '
                                                           "Commercial's role as originating "
                                                           'broker.',
                                                           '23.8\u2003Good Faith.\u2003Each Party '
                                                           'shall act in good faith in the '
                                                           'performance of this Agreement. The '
                                                           'Parties acknowledge that New Jersey '
                                                           'law implies a covenant of good faith '
                                                           'and fair dealing in every contract, '
                                                           'and this Section is intended to '
                                                           'confirm and not to limit that '
                                                           'covenant.',
                                                           '23.9\u2003No Third-Party '
                                                           'Beneficiaries.\u2003Except as '
                                                           'expressly provided in Sections 15.2 '
                                                           'and 19.9 and in Exhibit 2 and Exhibit '
                                                           '4, this Agreement confers no rights on '
                                                           'any Person other than the Parties.',
